# Chezmoi Managed Home

- Edit source in `{{ .chezmoi.sourceDir }}`, then apply; never edit managed home targets directly.
- Check ownership with `chezmoi managed <path>` or source mappings; prefer managing unmanaged targets.
- Sources: `~/airules` -> `exact_airules`; `~/.gitconfig` -> `dot_gitconfig.tmpl`; `~/.zshrc` -> `dot_zshrc.tmpl`;
  Git post-checkout -> `dot_config/git/exact_hooks/executable_post-checkout`.
- `dot_` -> leading dot; `.tmpl` -> Go template; `executable_` -> executable. Use templates only for host values/secrets;
  prefer app env vars plus env templates when `${VAR}` works. Use `exact_` for source-owned directories/subdirectories,
  not app roots containing credentials, state, or dependencies.
- Deleted managed files -> add target paths to `.chezmoiremove`; ensure `.chezmoiignore` permits removal on affected hosts.

## Task References

Paths below are relative to `~/airules/`; load only matching references.

- Package installs/moves/removals, manager manifests -> `chezmoi/packages.md`
- Shell/env/alias changes -> `chezmoi/shell.md`
- Setup scripts, script marking/removal -> `chezmoi/scripts.md`
- AI models -> shared `aiModels` roles in `.chezmoidata.toml` and README's AI model roles section

## Repository Work

- Keep reusable rules in `exact_airules/`; update the parent index for subfiles and `dot_config/opencode/AGENTS.md` for
  root topics. Apply changed rules and all shared AGENTS.md targets.
- Add permanent tests/mocks/fixtures only on request; use existing checks or temporary self-checks.
- Prefer config changes; explain maintenance costs before app patches/forks. Keep cleanup task-scoped.
- Before migration/cleanup, verify old files and live service state; source definitions are not deployment evidence.
  Ask if a relevant host is inaccessible. Assume one user/app state and one cleanup suffice; mention repeat cleanup
  in the summary and ask before adding it.
- Find `one-off:` comments and `one-off` script filenames, including hidden scripts. Remove proven obsolete scripts and
  temporary artifacts, preserving outputs and setup needed on future hosts. Verify affected hosts and future install/
  upgrade needs; a successful run alone is not proof. If proof/access is missing, ask before removal.
- OS-specific behavior and cleanup -> `general-coding.md`; Windows commands -> `windows.md`.

## Verification

- Check `chezmoi status` and `timeout 2 chezmoi diff`, then try `czapply` or `timeout 2 chezmoi apply -v` if unavailable.
  If full apply is unsafe, scope diff/apply to task targets. Verify applied state; report failures, timeouts, and remaining
  work. Ask the user to run `czapply` if needed.
- After commands, check `git status --short` for unexpected changes. After background processes, check `pty_list` and
  terminate task-owned sessions.
